## Problem classes

### `Peer missing on Windows`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Other platforms see this machine; Windows does not appear | Firewall blocked UDP 5353, or Bonsoir broadcast failed to start. Windows uses the same Bonsoir path (`DnsServiceRegister` / WinDNS). | Check the advertise log and the private-network firewall prompt. Manual connect remains if multicast is blocked. Do not put Windows back on a browse-only early return. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Nearby badge says Same LAN but transfers fail`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Subnet match treated as reachable | `/hello` never ran, or AP isolation drops the TCP path | Badge Same LAN only after `/hello` succeeds. Otherwise Other LAN or BLE only, per `proximity.mdc`. |

